# Stop all G:\ciel-Walkie background agents

## Request
Stop every background agent running in G:\ciel-walkie so the oldest original
session can take over, and identify that oldest session.

## Observed (before)
- `~/.claude/sessions/*.json` alive entries with cwd `G:\ciel-Walkie`:
  pid 61768 = bg 57d7eb89; pid 62424 = bg 589869b8 "m4 child retry verification (3)"
  (fork of transcript 8adb3585).
- Orphan `gh run watch 41377115224 --repo OneCiel/ciel-walkie` chain (parent gone).
- `claude agents --json` also held four `blocked` ciel-Walkie bg entries:
  4303f1a2, 93e600db, 026372b7, d2d44ee2.

## Actions
1. `taskkill /T /F` on the two pty-host trees and the gh chain. The daemon
   (pid 26224) respawned both sessions within seconds (ListAgents "started 0s ago"),
   so process kill alone does not stop a daemon-managed bg session.
2. `claude stop <id>` for 589869b8, 57d7eb89, 4303f1a2, 93e600db, 026372b7,
   d2d44ee2 — each printed `stopped <id>`.
3. Killed orphan `transcript-relay.py` pid 75152 left by the brief respawn.
4. Daemon 26224 left running: it also hosts the ciel-runtime sessions.

## Verified (after, +20s)
- Only process whose command line contains `ciel-walkie`: daemon 26224
  (via its `--spawned-by` label).
- No alive registry entry with cwd `G:\ciel-Walkie`.
- `claude agents --json`: no ciel-Walkie entries.
- ListAgents peers: gam-495-43 (GAM-495), ciel-socket-e2e (2) (ciel-runtime).

## Oldest original session
- `417ef30b-1289-47a5-8921-a4d45eb93f2e` — interactive, transcript
  `~/.claude/projects/G--ciel-Walkie/417ef30b-....jsonl`, created 2026-09-17 02:23,
  2,958,180,900 bytes, last write 2026-10-26 14:38. Registry runs: pid 88740
  (started 2026-10-22 11:27) and pid 92376 (2026-10-26 01:32), both not running.
- Resume: `cd G:\ciel-Walkie; claude --resume 417ef30b-1289-47a5-8921-a4d45eb93f2e`
  (not executed).
